meta {
  name: Register Application Document (Student)
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/application-forms/my-applications/{{applicationId}}/documents
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "documents": [
      {
        "document_type": "neet_scorecard",
        "file_url": "{{permanentUrl}}",
        "file_name": "scorecard.png",
        "file_size_bytes": 102400,
        "mime_type": "image/png"
      },
      {
        "document_type": "aadhaar_card",
        "file_url": "{{permanentUrl}}",
        "file_name": "aadhaar.pdf",
        "file_size_bytes": 204800,
        "mime_type": "application/pdf"
      }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Registers one or more uploaded files against document requirements on
  the student's own application in a single call — `documents` accepts
  1..N entries, each shaped like the old single-document body. Each file
  itself must already be uploaded via the existing generic student upload
  flow first: POST /api/v1/student/uploads/document/presign -> PUT to the
  returned uploadUrl -> POST /api/v1/student/uploads/document/verify -> use
  the returned permanentUrl as that entry's file_url.

  Every entry's `document_type` must match a document requirement
  currently applicable to this application (404 if any one isn't — e.g.
  inactive, or scoped to a course/quota/nationality the student doesn't
  have), and each entry's `mime_type` must be one of that requirement's
  acceptedMimeTypes (400 otherwise). The whole batch is validated before
  anything is written, so if any single entry is invalid, none of the
  documents in the request are saved.

  Two allowed states for the parent application:
  - `draft` — freely add/replace any document_type, exactly as before.
  - `submitted` — only allowed as a **resubmission of a rejected
    document**: every document_type in the batch must already have an
    uploaded row with verificationStatus "rejected" (409 ConflictError,
    naming the offending type, otherwise). This is how a student acts on
    college-admin's rejection after the application is finalized — no
    other edits are possible once submitted.
  Any other formStatus -> 409 ConflictError ("This application can no
  longer be edited").

  Upsert semantics (per entry): registering the same document_type again
  replaces the prior file (not a duplicate row) and resets
  verificationStatus back to "pending". A submitted-stage resubmission also
  increments resubmissionCount and leaves the document's verificationHistory
  untouched (it keeps every past rejection for the admin-side timeline).

  Response `data` is an array, one saved document per entry, in request order.
}
